          "title": "How to Identify Pure Handloom Silk",
          "excerpt": "Learn the simple burn test and texture checks to distinguish authentic handloom silk.",
          "body": "A pure handloom silk saree is not always perfectly even. Small variations in the weave are normal and are what make each piece one of a kind. A few simple checks can help you, none of them is proof on its own.\n\nTouch: real silk feels smooth but warm, and does not feel slippery like polyester.\nThe burn test: with the seller's permission, burn a loose thread only (never the saree). Real silk burns slowly, smells like burnt hair and leaves a soft ash you can crush. Synthetic thread melts, smells like plastic and leaves a hard bead.\nThe weaver: ask which cluster the saree comes from and look for the Silk Mark or the weaver's tag.\n\nIf a price looks too low for the work involved, be careful.",
          "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1594736797933-d0501ba2fe65?q=80&w=600",
          "alt": "Handloom silk",
          "show": true
        },
