          "id": "j3",
          "date": "2026-09-28",
          "title": "Preserving Your Heirloom Saree",
          "excerpt": "Essential tips on storage, cleaning, and maintenance to ensure your sarees last for generations.",
          "body": "A good saree can last for generations if it is stored well.\n\n• Keep it in a soft cotton or muslin cloth. Plastic traps moisture.\n• Refold along different lines every few months so the creases do not cut the zari.\n• Keep it away from direct sunlight and from perfume or hairspray.\n• Air it in the shade once a season.\n• Use naphthalene-free repellents, away from the cloth.\n• Send zari silks to a dry cleaner who knows handlooms; do not machine wash.\n\nIf a stain happens, blot (do not rub) and take it to a professional soon.",
